Korean consonants are broadly categorized into two categories:{{Sfn|Kim-Renaud|2009|pp=16–17}}

* [[Obstruent|obstruents]]: sounds produced when airflow either completely stops (i.e. a [[Stop consonant|plosive]] consonant) or passes through a narrow opening (i.e. a [[Fricative consonant|fricative]]).
* [[Sonorant|sonorants]]: sounds produced when air flows out with little to no obstruction through the mouth, nose, or both.

